To implement bubble sort in C++ with minimal memory usage and error avoidance, you can follow these steps:

1. Define a swap function that takes two pointers as arguments and swaps their values without allocating any new memory. This will help minimize memory usage and avoid potential errors caused by dynamic memory allocation.

```cpp
void swap(int *a, int *b) {
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}
